{"posts":[{"id":"aboutcompression_p32_776","t":"boy2boy wrote: Hi,\n\nGood,\n\nsome of them are wrong, you don't need to use rectangles but you still have to visualise them...\n\nCan u look at the other charts of yours and check if there are wrong CP's?\n\nLP","a":"Les_Paul","d":"","n":"#776","p":32,"im":["9b7e5a688ce7ad5db634457cf442d0f75e3a4ab9","19de9aa542243563041f5bcb37e3cbc2805e9092"],"m":776},{"id":"aboutcompression_p32_777","t":"Harry wrote: it was only for demonstration purposes, i wont do it again, i promise\n\nAm I doing anything wrong here?\n\nI though Paul asking me to do the same thing as well.","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#777","p":32,"im":[],"m":777},{"id":"aboutcompression_p32_778","t":"boy2boy wrote:\n\nHarry wrote: it was only for demonstration purposes, i wont do it again, i promise\n\nNo, u're doing great... just look at the CP's again, and check whether all Supply/Demand levels in them were tested...\n\nLP","a":"Les_Paul","d":"","n":"#778","p":32,"im":[],"m":778},{"id":"aboutcompression_p32_779","t":"boy2boy wrote: Hi,\n\nAre you aware of the standard marking of Compressed Zones? Pls start using it.\n\nHope I'm doing it correctly.\n\nRedo again on this","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#779","p":32,"im":["523c65b7c34855fe1f0959f5e396b9b6ca3cf43c","dac76c4f1f4ad5967930da02d5f5cd54fb11391d"],"m":779},{"id":"aboutcompression_p32_780","t":"boy2boy wrote:\n\nboy2boy wrote: Hi,\n\nAre you aware of the standard marking of Compressed Zones? Pls start using it.\n\nHope I'm doing it correctly.\n\nB2B! Congratulations, these are correct CP ZONES!\n\nLes_Paul","a":"Les_Paul","d":"","n":"#780","p":32,"im":["523c65b7c34855fe1f0959f5e396b9b6ca3cf43c","dac76c4f1f4ad5967930da02d5f5cd54fb11391d"],"m":780},{"id":"aboutcompression_p32_781","t":"boy2boy wrote: Hi,\n\nRedo\n\nLittle bit more difficult to spot on HTF - for me","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#781","p":32,"im":["c0e0b3ca665eb7b31c4c0e684d6961dbff44518f","d2eae619f293ffda53fdd2bf9bff517b049400a1"],"m":781},{"id":"abo